WEBVTT

00:00:00.920 --> 00:00:05.400
The storyboards in animated film field

00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:09.800
were really used to bring a written script

00:00:09.950 --> 00:00:13.290
into something that was pictorialized

00:00:13.290 --> 00:00:16.660
and pre-edited for film.

00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:22.780
And so in the early days at Hanna-Barbera,

00:00:23.210 --> 00:00:27.770
so many of the writers used to actually draw their scripts.

00:00:28.900 --> 00:00:29.960
They were almost like...

00:00:30.030 --> 00:00:39.180
comic strips and the job of the storyboard men was more as editors because indeed this is what

00:00:39.180 --> 00:00:47.540
they did. They broke them down into edited scenes and they redrew them so that they would stage

00:00:47.540 --> 00:00:52.970
well for on the screen for the animators and for the layout men.

00:01:02.910 --> 00:01:07.080
Who is the superhero?

00:01:08.050 --> 00:01:10.250
Sarge? No.

00:01:11.910 --> 00:01:13.790
Rosemary, the telephone operator?

00:01:16.560 --> 00:01:18.860
Henry, the mild-mannered janitor?

00:01:19.290 --> 00:01:20.110
Could be!

00:01:23.030 --> 00:01:23.750
Hooey!

00:01:24.170 --> 00:01:25.470
Number one super guy!

00:01:30.190 --> 00:01:34.480
He's got style, a groovy style, and a mob that just won't stop

00:01:34.700 --> 00:01:43.580
Up, he's the Hong Kong Pooey Chop, number one super guy

00:01:43.580 --> 00:01:51.240
Call Pooey Chop, take it goodbye

00:02:00.090 --> 00:02:00.450
VICK!

00:02:34.800 --> 00:02:37.020
I want that batty bank mob caught!

00:02:38.170 --> 00:02:42.360
You heard me. Caught. Captured. Incarcerated.

00:02:43.640 --> 00:02:46.550
Ooh, ooh, that's the third bank they've ripped off.

00:02:46.850 --> 00:02:48.070
And it better be the last.

00:02:48.500 --> 00:02:52.270
Hear me? The absolute positive last.

00:02:55.320 --> 00:02:56.620
Pen-ree-

00:02:57.380 --> 00:02:58.740
Sorry about that, Sergeant, sir.

00:02:59.090 --> 00:02:59.970
But come to think-

00:03:00.030 --> 00:03:02.570
You did order me to paint everything in the building.

00:03:04.020 --> 00:03:08.550
I agree that it's an improvement, Panry,

00:03:08.670 --> 00:03:11.210
but do you think Sergeant Flint will?

00:03:11.450 --> 00:03:12.970
Golly, Rosemary, you're right.

00:03:13.450 --> 00:03:15.390
I'd better give him a shot of paint remover.

00:03:17.520 --> 00:03:19.680
Boy, that's sure a strong paint remover.

00:03:20.210 --> 00:03:23.510
Rosemary, you got any idea who's robbing them banks?

00:03:24.140 --> 00:03:25.980
I'm not a detective, Panry,

00:03:26.060 --> 00:03:28.180
but as a brilliant and beautiful dispatcher,

00:03:28.180 --> 00:03:29.980
I'd say it's the baddie bank mo-

00:03:30.120 --> 00:03:32.810
Got any brilliant and beautiful clothes?

00:03:32.990 --> 00:03:36.670
No, but every bank they've robbed has been near the ocean.

00:03:37.240 --> 00:03:38.830
Uh, which ocean?

00:03:39.190 --> 00:03:41.270
How many oceans are there around here?

00:03:41.690 --> 00:03:44.350
Gee, Penry, all his sudden interest in crime.

00:03:45.060 --> 00:03:47.860
You were Hong Kong Fui or something.

00:03:48.930 --> 00:03:52.190
Time to change from humble, lovable Janet the Penry

00:03:52.190 --> 00:03:57.060
to that gigantic giant of goodness, Hong Kong Fui.

00:04:01.240 --> 00:04:07.070
No stuck drawer's gonna stick me, I'll super-strength it open on the count of three.

00:04:07.640 --> 00:04:09.760
A one, a two, a three.

00:04:15.430 --> 00:04:18.230
Sometimes it's not easy being a superhero.

00:04:19.090 --> 00:04:25.620
On with Fearless Polarist Cat, we're off to catch the Batty Bank Mob.

00:04:38.480 --> 00:04:41.500
I guess I must have parked my Fooie-mobile upside down!

00:04:44.800 --> 00:04:52.220
...on a bank.

00:04:52.790 --> 00:04:55.170
Now, if those crooks are robbing banks near the ocean,

00:04:55.650 --> 00:04:57.630
they're sent to try one named after.

00:04:57.850 --> 00:04:59.970
And there's the perfect hiding place to wait.

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:00.340
Oh

00:05:45.450 --> 00:05:47.920
must I tell you, Spot. It's two hands

00:05:47.920 --> 00:05:49.900
for catching and one for throwing.

00:06:03.070 --> 00:06:10.510
You know, boss, if you told someone we were going to use a sub to rob a bank, he'd say we were cuckoo.

00:06:10.700 --> 00:06:12.340
That's why we can't miss.

00:06:12.580 --> 00:06:15.560
The idea is so batty, it's brilliant.

00:06:19.520 --> 00:06:26.790
Best thing about this disguise is I can watch the bank and at the same time catch lunch for my faithful cat.

00:06:31.150 --> 00:06:38.810
Sure hope that batty bank mob shows up soon

00:06:38.810 --> 00:06:41.770
so I can catch them and get back to Peyton headquarters

00:06:41.770 --> 00:06:43.630
before the sergeant gets real mad.

00:06:44.730 --> 00:06:48.660
Think you're doing.

00:06:49.000 --> 00:06:50.520
Reckon I'll have to throw you back.

00:06:50.950 --> 00:06:52.550
Little submarines ain't in season.

00:06:56.770 --> 00:06:58.510
Get so uptight, friend spot.

00:06:58.860 --> 00:06:59.840
You couldn't eatin' that.

00:07:00.220 --> 00:07:23.810
the submarine. The man in the sub, swinger, he's a swinger. It's a bat. He belongs.

00:07:39.820 --> 00:07:42.680
I gotta remember to bong the gong before I float the boat.

00:07:45.260 --> 00:07:54.320
Fish for that submarine again!

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:06.020
He's kind of puny looking, ain't he?

00:08:17.680 --> 00:08:20.060
Hong Kong Foy thinks he's capturing us.

00:08:20.320 --> 00:08:21.920
I'll sneak out and capture him.

00:08:30.060 --> 00:08:32.920
Let's see what it says about underwater Kung Fu.

00:08:33.350 --> 00:08:34.790
Ah, this should get him.

00:08:35.180 --> 00:08:37.700
The crab crawl with a lobster lurch.

00:08:39.540 --> 00:08:53.220
He's caught in the rocks.

00:08:53.670 --> 00:08:55.470
But superheroes are never too busy

00:08:55.470 --> 00:08:57.430
to help a animu in distress.

00:09:00.730 --> 00:09:09.740
Well, am I supposed to catch crooks if the minute they see me coming, they run?

00:09:11.340 --> 00:09:12.160
How about that?

00:09:12.340 --> 00:09:14.540
He wants to give me a piggyback ride.

00:09:14.910 --> 00:09:18.070
Or what you call it, a octopus back ride.

00:09:22.970 --> 00:09:27.630
That gang's so underhanded, we'll have to take our foley boat underwater to get him.

00:09:34.380 --> 00:09:35.960
I wonder where them crooks went.

00:09:37.650 --> 00:09:39.650
Well, it's my little friend, the octopus.

00:09:40.190 --> 00:09:42.950
He wants us to follow him.

00:09:56.770 --> 00:09:59.970
My guess is they're using this tunnel to blast their way into the back.

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:06.500
If you ask me, that was a pretty close guess.

00:10:10.100 --> 00:10:10.960
Phooey, I get...

00:10:11.620 --> 00:10:15.560
Mr. Batty Bank Bandit, I arrest you in the name of the law.

00:10:15.880 --> 00:10:17.020
You're not the law.

00:10:17.520 --> 00:10:20.180
Then, I'll arrest you in the name of my name.

00:10:24.080 --> 00:10:24.840
It's wrong.

00:10:25.290 --> 00:10:28.910
You fellas are supposed to be scared stiff at the mere sight of me.

00:10:29.460 --> 00:10:29.960
Then take...

00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:34.020
It takes more than one Hong Kong phooey to stop the batty bank mob.

00:10:34.260 --> 00:10:37.820
But there's just two of you. That doesn't make a game.

00:10:38.140 --> 00:10:40.270
No, but they do.

00:10:42.720 --> 00:10:45.480
I'll just check my Hong Kong Book of Kung Fu.

00:10:45.940 --> 00:10:48.040
Here it is, How to Stop a Game.

00:10:48.300 --> 00:10:50.040
It says, go get help.

00:10:51.060 --> 00:10:54.000
Well, there ain't time for that, so I'll just help myself.

00:11:14.620 --> 00:11:20.810
I blocked the baddie sub, and I did it the hard way, with my head covered.

00:11:25.020 --> 00:11:27.330
Yep, the way I planned it.

00:11:28.020 --> 00:11:29.970
Cut off the crooks' escape, and then have...

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:38.360
the police run in and make the arrest and while they're running in i'll be running back to the

00:11:38.360 --> 00:11:44.730
headquarters to finish paint come on spot i'll show you how to practice kung fu on the gallop
